# Build output from `make build` / `make all`. The source is the Go files; these
# are the compiled hub binary and headless flasher, regenerated on demand.
bin/

# An ad-hoc `go build` run from this directory ignores those redirects and writes the
# binary here, named after the package: the hub itself plus every cmd/ main. Anchored,
# and one name per binary: a glob like /orb* would swallow the tracked orbcmd.go.
/orb-manager
/orbflash
/orbfake
/orbpack
/orbprobe
/orbvendor
/serprov

# Do NOT ignore internal/firmware/bundle/*.zip or web/composer/*. That pair is
# the firmware and the Theme Editor compiled into the binary — committed on
# purpose, so `make build` works with no ESP-IDF and a downloaded .exe flashes an
# orb with no clone on disk. Refresh them with `make firmware` / `make composer`.
